Kent Paul Dolan wrote:
> How I'd like some one of my buffed up PCs not to end
> up as cannon fodder, after almost 19 years
> unascended. So, I'm seeking advice for my current
> incarnation.

Hello, Kent.

First observation: For all your buffing up, I notice you have no source
of magic resistance whatsoever.

You need to fix this ASAP.  You're intensely vulnerable to touch of
death or armor destruction.

2. You have a decent melee weapon,  and some good range weapons. This
is good.
3. Am I correct in guessing that almost all your AC reduction is from
your armor?
If you have not done so already, find a peaceful priest and start
dumping gold on him in shots of 400 * XL < your donation < 600 * XL
4.  You have little in the way of light sources. I would recommend
learning it as a spell.  Light keeps me alive where nothing else
does... keeps me from blundering into critters in the dark.
5. What are your resistances and intrinsics? Do you have fire
resistance, shock resistance, cold resistance, sleep resistance,
disintegration resistance?  If you do not, get 'em.
6. fight ochre jellies at a distance.  Also mumaks. Lost good,
promising characters to them.
7. How many pets do you have?   There's nothing like having a pack of
dogs -- unless it's a pack of archons -- and a magic whistle. You can
use tripe rations as a cheap 'charm monster'.

8. your hit points could be higher. Consider quaffing ! of extra
healing. I would avoid nurse dancing.

9. I see you have no wands.   Recommend saving wands of fire, wands of
lightning, wands of digging, and wands of teleport.

Wands of fire can be used to engrave "Elbereth" in 1 turn. Also, the
engraving made with a wand of fire will last forever. You would be
amazed how often this will save your life.

Wands of lightning engrave in 1 turn, last a real long time, but blind
you.

Wands of digging write in 1 turn,  are common as dirt in Gehenna, and
the engraving will
last for a few turns.

Wands of teleport are almost as good as wands of death -- they work on
anything, they hardly ever miss,  and whatever you're shooting at is
going to stop being an immediate problem. In some ways it's better than
a wand of death, because a teleport wand will work on vampires, liches,
and demons which a wand of death will not.

Of course, you will have to fight the creature again, but it will stop
bothering for a few turns ... possibly quite a few if it was sent to
the other end of the dungeon.  You can then
take it on after you've solved your immediate problems, and instead of
being swarmed it is a one-on-one unfair fight.  Or just run away, going
around it to the stairs.

10. I see no means of levitation.  Get one -- not only is it useful on
the planes of air and fire, but if you use it a lot you can float over
trap doors, pits and such like.

11. Consider getting boots of water walking.  Then you can walk on a
moat and dip as many potions as you like in the moat and it'll never
dry out. I get 40-50 potions of water that way (which, of course,
become Holy water in short order).

12. I notice none of your stuff is rustproofed. If you want to keep it,
you should do that so a rust monster won't eat it. If it's made of
cloth or wood it should be fireproofed so it won't be destroyed by fire
traps.

How  to rust proof?  Well, you can read a scroll of enchant armor while
confused or read a CURSED scroll of destroy armor while confused.   The
CURSED scroll of destroy armor will only rustproof your equipment,
while enchant armor will not only rustproof it but repair any damage to
it as well.

13. Consider using a hard gem to engrave "Elbereth" at strategic points
on any level -- it takes 8 turns but A) the engraving will last awhile
and B) a hard gem never wears out or goes dull like a dagger does.  You
can then use these as "safety spots" like the base in a game of hide
and seek.


13. How have your last five characters died?  If you can answer that
question here, we can probably see what you're doing wrong.  You may
not even need to ask us ... what's the common theme?

14. A suggestion that helps me the most ... it's a tactic ...

BE A COWARD.

Let your pets do the fighting for you.  Use polearms.  Use ranged
weapons.  Run away. Engrave "Elbereth". Drop scrolls of scare monster.
Read scrolls of teleportation. Zap the floor underneath you with a wand
of digging and fall to the next level.  Zap the wall and go through the
wall. Zap a wand of teleport at bad guys to make them go away.  Zap it
at yourself to escape.  Do anything and everything you reasonably can
to avoid melee combat.   Consider playing a rogue or a ranger to get
used to that playing style.

15. Remember ... this is a TURN-based game.

Your single greatest advantage is not your +7 artifact weapon, is not
your Wand of Mass Destruction, is not your +35 Chromatic Dragon Scale
Mail.  Your greatest advantage in a dungeon where you are outnumbered
5,000 to 1 is the gray matter on top of your shoulders ... and ALL THE
TIME IN THE WORLD to use it.

So ... if you get in a jam, STOP!  Walk away from the computer. Smoke a
cigarette or eat a twinkie.  Watch a movie.  Let your blood settle
down.  THEN come back, look at your inventory,  sit down with a paper
and pencil, and THINK your way out of your predicament.

NOTHING HAPPENS UNTIL YOU PRESS A KEY.   You have as much time as you
like.  Use all of it.   Your greatest advantage is something you'll
never have in real combat ... the luxury to think through your
situation.

And if you're dying often from blundering into things in the corridors,
the time has come to start thinking between moves as well ...  press a
"move key", count to five mississippi, then press a movement key again.
Don't simply run around like this was DOOM or an archlich will
touch-of-death you to eternity before you even know he's there.

This is going to sound silly ... but 19 years?  Adding you to my prayer
list.  Usually reserve it for emergencies like surgeries and so forth,
but I think this qualifies.

Hope some of this helps.  

